+
+## Ground-H fragment continuation: package v8
+
+`H-1s-ionization-20261029.json` is a **separate ground-state atomic-H target**
+freeze. Water data v7 remain byte-identical. Official NIST1s constants are
+B=U=13.6057eV, N=1 and Q=0.5668. The general Q-dependent BEB Eq1 is used with
+the same NIST a0/R constants; the more detailed BED secondary spectrum is not
+imported. Seven65-digit Decimal formula evaluations are computational oracles,
+not measured cross sections or a claim of reproducing the online CGI outputs.
+
+`hydrogen_fragment_ionization.h` exposes `HydrogenFragmentIonizationData::read`,
+`ionization_cross_section_m2(E_target_rest_eV)`, physical-weight `coverage`, and
+`strict_rate_m3_s`. Positive rate/event support is **14-10000eV**. Energies
+at/below13.59844eV have a known forbidden ionization reference; the unresolved
+positive13.59844-14eV threshold interval and all energies above10keV are refused,
+never filled with zero or endpoint-held. Uncovered electrons stay in the rate
+denominator. The source's general near1keV model accuracy is not promoted into
+a new10keV error guarantee.
+
+`conditional_H1s_ionization_products(data,"H1s_NIST_BEB_equal_pair_CM_v1",
+E_eV,W,MH,beam_unit,CM_e_pair_unit)` returns `ConditionalParentProducts` for
+e+H(1s)->2e+Hplus. With only one bound target electron, its ionization products
+have no molecular-fragment branching ambiguity. The equal-energy back-to-back
+CM pair and proton-at-rest-CM law remain an explicit differential comparison
+assumption, with exact relativistic boost/recoil. This is ground protium only;
+the API rejects molecular/deuterium-scale target masses.
+
+The host debits **one atomic H**, not a water parent, and replaces the incident
+electron with two outgoing electrons at matched weight W. The actual H(1s)
+inventory supplies its target density. H and water hazards can compete for
+the same PIC electrons without introducing another electron inventory.
+The proton mass MH-me+13.59844eV/c2 matches the existing shared source-rounded
+water fragment catalog. Count chemical reference once per physical H event;
+scale every returned kinetic/reference energy by W once. Host ownership of
+cohort splitting, RNG, transforms, deposition and atomic rollback is unchanged.
+
+Run `tools/test_hydrogen_fragment.sh` for its pinned CPU7/one-thread checks.
+`h2o-collision-port-v8.json` declares both immutable datasets and the new target
+contract. This does not supply H excitation/elastic scattering, recombination,
+other fragment targets or the remaining water mechanism. Source leads for
+vibrational-ground H2Oplus dissociative recombination are retained externally;
+their thermal coefficients are not substituted for nonthermal PIC rates.
